course: dictionary
lesson: 9041
title: Slavic words and families
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Slavic is a word you may meet in geography, history and language lessons. It means about the Slavs, a large group of peoples in eastern and central Europe, or about their languages. When it is written with a capital S, as in Slavic countries, it is an adjective, and it describes a thing.
explain: Languages can be related like a family. «Ukrainian, Polish and Czech are cousins in the Slavic family» means these languages grew from the same roots, so many of their words look alike. English, German and Dutch are cousins in the Germanic family, and «water» and «Wasser» show that cousins can look alike.
explain: Slavic can also be a noun, meaning the group of languages itself. Ukrainian, Polish, Czech, Russian, Bulgarian and Serbian are all Slavic languages. Ask yourself: is the word describing something, or naming the group? That tells you which part of speech it is.
explain: Words can travel between languages too. «Borscht», the beetroot soup closely linked to Ukraine, reached English through Yiddish from the Slavic word «борщ». Look at the letters: «борщ» is written in Cyrillic, which many Slavic languages use. Polish and Czech use the Latin alphabet instead.
fact: Slavic means about the Slavs, or about their languages.
fact: Slavic is written with a capital S, like other names of peoples and languages.
fact: Slavic languages are a family of related languages, such as Ukrainian, Polish, Czech, Russian, Bulgarian and Serbian.
fact: Many Slavic languages use the Cyrillic alphabet, but Polish and Czech use the Latin alphabet.
fact: Languages in one family are like cousins: they share roots, so their words can look alike.
exercise: «Ukrainian, Polish and Czech are cousins in the Slavic family.» Which of these is a Slavic language? | Dutch | Spanish | *Polish | German
exercise: What does Slavic mean? | About a soup made from beetroot | About the Scandinavian leaders who came to rule Kyiv | Only the Latin alphabet | *About the Slavs, a large group of peoples in eastern and central Europe, or about their languages
exercise: «Spanish, French and Italian all grew from Latin.» Find and copy one word that names a family of languages in this sentence. | French | *Latin | Italian | Spanish
test: Which alphabet do Polish and Czech use? | Greek | *Latin | Cyrillic | Japanese
test: Is Spanish a Slavic language? | Only in Russia | Yes, it is a Slavic language | Yes, because it has the word Slavic in its name | *No, it grew from Latin
exam: Which word names the family of languages that Ukrainian, Polish and Czech belong to? | Cyrillic | Latin | *Slavic | Germanic
